|lore=The bones of a tauntaun represent both death and life: death for the prey, life for the predator. A symbol of the ebb and flow of the Force through all things.
|game_text=Deploy on table. Your ferocious creatures are deploy -2 and ferocity +2. Once per turn, may take a Tauntaun or a ferocious creature into hand from Reserve Deck; reshuffle. Twice per game, may deploy a Tauntaun or a ferocious creature from under your Starting Effect. (Immune to Alter.)
|printings={{Card versions/Tauntaun Bones (Hoth)}}
|notes=The 2006 slip keeps the same twice-per-game deployment from under Starting Effect as the launch slip. The [[Tauntaun Bones (V) (Virtual Set 4: Battle Of Hoth) (Original)|original-edition slip]] survives in the exact release PDF created on 4 February 2003. The sheet gives 5 February as the sanctioned legality date. The [[Tauntaun Bones (V) (Virtual Set 4: Battle Of Hoth) (Remastered 2006)|2006 publication]] gives its text as of 4 December 2006. [https://www.theforce.net/ccg/story/Star_Wars_CCG_Virtual_Set_4_Press_Release_63874.asp 22 January 2003 publisher press preview].
|sources=* [https://web.archive.org/web/20071024153629/http://www.swccgpc.com/Resources/VirtualCards4.pdf#page=3 VirtualCards4.pdf] (Players Committee Remaster sheet, Internet Archive 24 October 2007) — official text as of 4 December 2006; page 3, slip 19. Slip image and game text from this sheet.
* Lore and art: the printed Decipher card, [[Tauntaun Bones]].
* Full-card remaster: [[Virtual Set 4: Battle Of Hoth#Cards|Virtual Set 4: Battle Of Hoth]] (fan reconstruction, 2026).
